    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented for the soft-delete change:\n\n## Changes\n\n**1. `Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) defaulting to `false`, with getter/setter. A newly created owner is therefore `false` by default.\n\n**2. `DeleteOwner` function** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`) \u2014 changed from a hard `repository.delete(owner)` to a soft-delete: sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner, retaining the row. The existing `DELETE.yml` pipeline (Load \u2192 Delete \u2192 RespondWithNoContent, 204) is unchanged and still returns 2xx.\n\n**3. Create-path checks** \u2014 both now skip soft-deleted owners:\n- `EnsureUniqueHousehold.java` \u2014 the blocking duplicate check ignores deleted owners, so a normally-blocking household duplicate is allowed when the only match is deleted.\n- `FlagPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 the identity/possible-duplicate flag ignores deleted owners.\n\n**4. API schema** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it; `GET` now reports `deleted`. It's on the response schema only (not `OwnerFields`), so the create request body doesn't accept it.\n\n**5. DB schemas** \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN ... DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). HSQLDB requires `DEFAULT` before `NOT NULL`, which was the one syntax wrinkle I hit and fixed.\n\nVerification: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` both pass, and the full `mvnw test` run reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (2 tests, 0 failures/errors).",
